-- ─── Clean text: one list, every surface ─────────────────────────────
-- Generated by scripts/blocked-terms-sql.mjs from src/lib/blockedTerms.json.
-- Edit the JSON, regenerate into a new migration, apply. Do not edit the
-- rows below by hand: a test compares them with the JSON.
--
-- Every term carries a severity: 3 hate (slurs, hate slogans, harassment),
-- 2 obscene, 1 crude. A "name" surface (usernames, display names, bios,
-- room titles, community names, post titles) refuses every term. A "body"
-- surface (post bodies, comments, room chat, community descriptions and
-- rules, the room frame) refuses severity >= app_config
-- clean_body_min_severity (default 2: obscene and hate; set 3 to let
-- swearing through while slurs stay refused).
--
-- find_blocked_term folds the text the way src/lib/cleanText.ts does:
-- NFKD without accents, lowercase, lookalike letters to Latin, ß→ss,
-- punctuation glued to a word dropped, leetspeak to letters, spaced-out
-- single letters joined; then variants with short chunks joined to their
-- neighbours and repeated letters squeezed. A term must match as a whole
-- word; a phrase matches with or without separators between its words.
-- The two-tiny-chunk variant ("sh it") only counts for severity >= 2, so
-- "an Al" is a name and not a body part.
--
-- The gate is a trigger on each table, checking only the columns that
-- changed, raising errcode 22023 with hint blocked_term and a message the
-- UI can show as is. set_config('agora.skip_clean', 'on', true) skips it
-- for imports and backfills. Historical rows are left alone.

